## File inventory + security scan

```sh
# Wrote forensic/phase2b-5/scripts/build-inventory.ts
bun run forensic/phase2b-5/scripts/build-inventory.ts
# Output: Inventory: 924 files | sensitive: 0 | categories: {data:725, report:126, source:60, log:8, test:4, other:1}

# Broad security scan (grep for github_pat_, ghp_, gho_, sk-, AKIA, FIREWORKS_API_KEY=, OPENAI_API_KEY=, Authorization: Bearer)
# → false positives only (research/legal_opc*.json "mask-" substring; skills/*.html base64 image data)
# Precise scan on Writing OS artifacts only:
grep -rEw "github_pat_..." corpus src/corpus tests/corpus writing-engine docs/corpus forensic/phase2b-5 logs43fw   # clean
grep -rE "ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}" corpus src/corpus tests/corpus writing-engine docs/corpus forensic/phase2b-5 logs43fw   # clean
grep -rE "FIREWORKS_API_KEY=[\"'][^\"']{10,}" ...   # clean
grep -rE "Authorization:\s*Bearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9_\.\-]{20,}" ...   # clean
grep -rE "BEGIN (RSA |EC |OPENSSH |PGP )?PRIVATE KEY" ...   # clean
find ... -name ".env*"   # clean
# All scans saved to forensic/phase2b-5/intermediate/security-scan*.txt
```

