## Git commit + push

```sh
git checkout research/phase2b-golden-corpus-v1-reconciled
git add corpus/ src/corpus/ tests/corpus/ writing-engine/logs-golden-v1/ docs/corpus/ forensic/phase2b-5/
git status   # verify staged files
git commit -m "fix(corpus): Phase 2B.5 — provenance model, 20 checks, GC-0038R1 ground-truth correction, forensic snapshot"
# Update MANIFEST.json head field to post-commit SHA
git add forensic/phase2b-5/MANIFEST.json
git commit --amend --no-edit   # OR second commit
git log --oneline -3
git ls-tree -r HEAD --name-only | grep forensic/phase2b-5/ | head   # verify forensic files in tree
git push origin research/phase2b-golden-corpus-v1-reconciled
```

## Notes

- **No API keys appear in any command.** The evaluator reads `FIREWORKS_API_KEY` from the env at runtime; the var name appears in source code and scan patterns, but never its value.
- **No `git push --force` used.** Plain push to the target branch.
- **No `main` modifications.** All commits go to `research/phase2b-golden-corpus-v1-reconciled`.
- **No `git add .` blind staging.** Explicit `git add` of specific directories.
